# Rank 1783 / CVE-2014-3527 (SEC-2688, CWE-346 origin validation; the nearest
# shipped concepts record CWE-20/918):
# spring-projects/spring-security's CAS proxy-ticket authentication takes the
# service URL -- the audience the CAS server matches a presented ticket
# against -- from `ServiceAuthenticationDetails.getServiceUrl()`.
# DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails
# (cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/
# DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java:53 at the parent) assembles it as
#
#   this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(request.getScheme(),
#           request.getServerName(), request.getServerPort(),
#           request.getRequestURI(), query);
#
# with `query` the request's query string minus the artifact (ticket)
# parameter. The servlet container resolves all three authority accessors from
# the client's own Host header, so the client picks the audience a proxy ticket
# is validated for: a ticket minted for a service the attacker controls
# validates as genuine. The fixed revision's own regression test names the
# property (`getServiceUrlDoesNotUseHostHeader`, `request.setServerName
# ("evil.com")` must still yield `https://example.com/...`).
#
# 934937d9c1dc20c396b96c08310b72cfa627acbf fixes it by parsing the configured
# service (`new URL(casService)`) and taking protocol, host and port from that
# URL instead, while `request.getRequestURI()` and the cleaned query still come
# from the request -- the path legitimately mirrors the request, the authority
# must not. ServiceProperties.afterPropertiesSet() also drops the
# `authenticateAllArtifacts` exemption so a configured `service` is mandatory,
# and ServiceAuthenticationDetailsSource grows a ServiceProperties constructor
# plus an ApplicationContextAware fallback. The remediation is present at the
# commit and absent at its parent f50e058d0, so both halves of the 1390 check
# hold and the pool row is correct in every field; no correction needed.
#
# What fires today, rechecked against the current knowledge base. `timeout 180
# ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB` over spring-security/cas, three
# runs per side, is byte-identical within each revision: 3 findings and 20
# flags at the parent, 3 findings and 21 flags at the fixed revision -- all
# three findings VYQL-INJ-009 log formatting in CasAuthenticationFilter, the
# flags core.AuthenticationCheck, and the one flag delta a core.ResourceRelease
# on `context.close` inside the fix's own new regression test. Nothing in
# DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java or
# ServiceAuthenticationDetailsSource.java on either side, in the findings view
# or the `-flags only` view. `vyql match` on the class labels
# `request.getRequestURI()` and `request.getQueryString()` as code.HttpInput
# and leaves getScheme/getServerName/getServerPort unlabelled;
# UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl is unbound.
#
# The host-header vocabulary shipped since the first pin does not reach this
# shape: UnvalidatedHostHeaderDispatch (VYQL-VAL-037) is a presence fact on a
# server transport's dispatch method (getRequestHeaders + Headers.HOST +
# Connectors.executeRootHandler -- Undertow's spelling, absent here), and
# requestHostUrlValidationBypass66 requires the compare form (getServerName +
# getHost + equals), which the assembly form spells neither half of.
#
# The discriminating taint route -- an authority-specific source on the three
# accessors, a sink on the CAS validate audience argument -- was probed with
# throwaway bindings for both ends over cas plus web (so UrlUtils resolves):
# zero at CasAuthenticationProvider.java:140. The chain dead-ends at three
# measured hops, each isolated below with shipped labels only (d)-(g):
#   1. a `this.`-qualified Java field store never feeds the matching load --
#      the same request read through a local reports VYQL-INJ-009, through a
#      bare-identifier field pair (`saved = ...; f(saved)`) also reports, and
#      through `this.saved = ...; f(this.saved)` is silent, in one method,
#      same statements; the trace shows the source dead-ending with no
#      outgoing node at all. The mixed spellings the real code uses --
#      `this.serviceUrl = ...` in a constructor with a bare `return
#      serviceUrl` getter -- are silent both same-method and across the
#      constructor/getter boundary. The write branch
#      (internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go:4821, `flow(args[0],
#      elemNode(recvNode, attr.Attr))`) and the bare-read slot
#      (`lowering.go:3668`, the class-member Name path) key different slots
#      for the same field. The rank-1198 entry filed the cross-method form
#      for PHP; in Java the this-qualified spelling fails intraprocedurally.
#   2. the interface routing shipped for the rank-1339 gap
#      (`resolveDerivedMethods`, internal/extract/lowering/lowering.go)
#      carries arguments into implementor bodies but an implementor's return
#      does not reach the caller's dispatch result -- `vyql trace` dead-ends
#      at `analysis.function.return`.
#   3. a cast-expression receiver (`((SavedSource) source).saved(request)`,
#      the consumer's exact spelling at CasAuthenticationProvider.java:162)
#      does not dispatch at all; the plain interface-typed variable is the
#      form the 1339 routing fixed.
# All three are new dataflow relations rather than mechanical corrections --
# field store-to-load is solver-wide and precision-costly by the same reasoning
# as 1198's entry -- so the rank is held.
#
# The presence route stays measured-unshippable, restated from the first pin
# and unchanged: the three accessors are the servlet API's documented
# request-mirroring idiom (~52 functions across 19 Java trees under
# /tmp/cve-work/rank*/, every one a correct mirror; in spring-security itself
# the vulnerable constructor plus UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl, DefaultSavedRequest
# and LoginUrlAuthenticationEntryPoint); adding a URL-assembly call narrows to
# 7 functions over 4 trees of which six are correct mirrors or origin checks
# (CorsUtils.isCorsRequest, ShiroHttpServletResponse.doIsEncodeable); a
# java.util.regex.Pattern-typed parameter is a rarity filter blind to the
# idiomatic getRequestURL() spelling; class-scope excision co-membership fails
# on openam's 2700-line SAML2Utils; ServiceAuthenticationDetails has exactly
# one implementation in the ecosystem scanned. A plain code.HttpInput source
# cannot discriminate either: the fixed revision still flows
# request.getRequestURI() into the same assembly, so only an
# authority-specific source separates the revisions, and that vocabulary's
# only instance is this fix.
#
# The cases: (a) and (b) are the two real revisions and record the miss; (c)
# is the request-mirror idiom the flaw half cannot be separated from, and must
# stay a reject -- a rule that fired on it would flag correct code throughout
# any servlet application; (d)-(h) isolate the consumer-side hops with the
# shipped HttpInput source and LogOutput sink: (d) is the positive control
# through a local and reports today, while (e) the this-qualified field
# store-to-load, (f) the implementor return through an interface-typed
# receiver, (g) the cast-receiver spelling of the same call and (h) the real
# code's own constructor-write/getter-return spelling are silent. When those
# hops carry, (e)-(h) flip to expect while (b) and (c) stay reject.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, cases (a) and (e)-(h) rejected.

test "rank1783: (a) the CAS service URL -- the audience a proxy ticket validates against -- is assembled from the request's own scheme, host and port"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import java.util.regex.Pattern;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import org.springframework.security.web.util.UrlUtils;

  final class DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails implements ServiceAuthenticationDetails {
    private final String serviceUrl;

    DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails(HttpServletRequest request, Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = getQueryString(request, artifactPattern);
      this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(request.getScheme(),
              request.getServerName(), request.getServerPort(),
              request.getRequestURI(), query);
    }

    public String getServiceUrl() {
      return serviceUrl;
    }

    private String getQueryString(final HttpServletRequest request, final Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = request.getQueryString();
      if (query == null) {
        return null;
      }
      final String result = artifactPattern.matcher(query).replaceFirst("");
      if (result.length() == 0) {
        return null;
      }
      return result.startsWith("&") ? result.substring(1) : result;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1783: (b) the fixed revision takes protocol, host and port from the configured service URL, keeping only the request's path and cleaned query"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import java.net.MalformedURLException;
  import java.net.URL;
  import java.util.regex.Pattern;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import org.springframework.security.web.util.UrlUtils;

  final class DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails implements ServiceAuthenticationDetails {
    private final String serviceUrl;

    DefaultServiceAuthenticationDetails(String casService, HttpServletRequest request, Pattern artifactPattern)
        throws MalformedURLException {
      URL casServiceUrl = new URL(casService);
      int port = getServicePort(casServiceUrl);
      final String query = getQueryString(request, artifactPattern);
      this.serviceUrl = UrlUtils.buildFullRequestUrl(casServiceUrl.getProtocol(),
              casServiceUrl.getHost(), port,
              request.getRequestURI(), query);
    }

    public String getServiceUrl() {
      return serviceUrl;
    }

    private static int getServicePort(URL casServiceUrl) {
      int port = casServiceUrl.getPort();
      if (port == -1) {
        port = casServiceUrl.getDefaultPort();
      }
      return port;
    }

    private String getQueryString(final HttpServletRequest request, final Pattern artifactPattern) {
      final String query = request.getQueryString();
      if (query == null) {
        return null;
      }
      final String result = artifactPattern.matcher(query).replaceFirst("");
      if (result.length() == 0) {
        return null;
      }
      return result.startsWith("&") ? result.substring(1) : result;
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1783: (c) the same three accessors in their documented role -- mirroring the request the client actually made -- which a rule on the accessors alone cannot be separated from"
  lang java
  file cas/src/main/java/org/springframework/security/cas/web/authentication/UrlUtils.java
  reject VYQL-RF-010
  reject VYQL-AUTH-003
  reject VYQL-RF-045
  code
  ```
  package org.springframework.security.cas.web.authentication;

  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;

  public final class UrlUtils {
    public static String buildFullRequestUrl(HttpServletRequest r) {
      return buildFullRequestUrl(r.getScheme(), r.getServerName(), r.getServerPort(), r.getRequestURI(),
              r.getQueryString());
    }

    public static String buildFullRequestUrl(String scheme, String serverName, int serverPort, String requestURI,
            String queryString) {
      scheme = scheme.toLowerCase();
      boolean includePort = true;
      if (serverPort == (scheme.equals("http") ? 80 : 443)) {
        includePort = false;
      }
      return scheme + "://" + serverName + (includePort ? ":" + serverPort : "") + requestURI
              + (queryString == null ? "" : "?" + queryString);
    }
  }
  ```

